     Layer 4 — Statistical Anomaly Detection

     Context

     The pipeline currently ships Layers 1 (Docling/VLM ingestion), 2
     (extraction/normalisation), 3 (Pydantic validation), and 5 (FastAPI +
     in-memory repo). Layer 4 (anomaly detection) is referenced by
     docs/architecture.md and docs/runtime.md (the /ingest/upload contract lists
     "extraction + validation + anomaly code loaded" as a hard dep in demo
     mode), but no implementation exists yet.

     The intended outcome of this change:
     - After a record is validated, run two unsupervised detectors (Isolation
     Forest + ECOD) on salaire_brut against a per-department baseline built from
     previously-uploaded records already in the in-memory repository.
     - Surface every anomaly as a Flag(moteur="anomaly", detail=..., score=...)
     row — never mutate RecStatus (human-in-the-loop: the reviewer reads the
     score + reason and decides).
     - Cold-start gracefully: when fewer than MIN_COHORT_SIZE (default 5)
     records exist for a departement, emit anomaly_baseline_unavailable instead
     of a meaningless score.

     User decisions captured in this turn:
     - Baseline scope: per-department, in-memory only.
     - Detector set: Isolation Forest + ECOD (parameter-free, stable on small
     cohorts).
     - Status impact: flags only, never mutate RecStatus.

