     New modules — app/anomalies/

     - app/anomalies/__init__.py — exports the public seam (run_anomaly_check,
     AnomalyScore).
     - app/anomalies/score.py — AnomalyScore dataclass (cohort: str, score: 
     float, reason: str, detector: str, consensus: bool). Also
     AnomalyCheckOutcome enum: ANOMALOUS, NOT_ANOMALOUS, BASELINE_UNAVAILABLE.
     - app/anomalies/baseline.py — builds the per-department cohort from
     IngestionJobRepository:
       - build_baseline(repository: IngestionJobRepository, min_cohort_size: int
     = 5) -> dict[str, list[float]] — returns departement -> [salaire_brut, 
     ...].
       - Reads repository._jobs.values() (private attr — acceptable here; the
     in-memory repo is intentionally a seam for swapping in Postgres), extracts
     HRRecord payloads with a parseable salaire_brut and departement, groups by
     department.
       - Records with missing salaire_brut or departement are skipped (they
     cannot contribute to the salary distribution).
     - app/anomalies/detectors.py — two thin wrappers over PyOD:
       - class IsolationForestDetector — uses pyod.models.iforest.IForest,
     contamination=0.1, random_state=42 (deterministic). .score(value, baseline:
